          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong coherent category
            (also called a
            = succeed ")" do
              %strong
                pre-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logos"} logos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular category
            in which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+posets"} subobject posets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub(X)
            all have finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unions"} unions
            which are preserved by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            functors
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*:Sub(Y)\to Sub(X)
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+functor"} coherent functor
            serves as a morphism between coherent categories.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            of a coherent category is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+logic"} coherent logic
          %p
            An
            %strong infinitary coherent category
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular category
            in which the subobject posets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub(X)
            have all
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+set"} small
            unions which are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+stability"} stable under pullback
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+category"} geometric categories
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-powered+category"} well-powered
          %p
            See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/familial+regularity+and+exactness"} familial regularity and exactness
            for a general description of the spectrum from regular categories through finitary and infinitary coherent categories.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                is a coherent category.
            %li
              %p
                More generally, any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
                is coherent and any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopos"} pretopos
                is coherent.
            %li
              %p
                Even more generally, any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+category"} locally cartesian closed category
                with finite
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
                is coherent, and thus any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasitopos"} quasitopos
                is coherent.
            %li
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+category"} Heyting category
                is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+category"} coherent category
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is coherent, so is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^D
                for any
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
                of a coherent category is coherent.
            %li
              %p
                Any
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+lattice"} distributive lattice
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thin+category"} thin category
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+PERs"} category of PERs
                over a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PCA"} PCA
                is coherent.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#extensivity Extensivity
          %p
            Any coherent category automatically has a strict
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
            of two subobjects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\hookrightarrow X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\hookrightarrow X
            such that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi B
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\cap B = 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⨿
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = A\amalg B
            is their
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+coproduct"} disjointly
            in some third object, then a coherent category has disjoint finite coproducts and is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensive+category"} extensive
            (or “positive”).
          %p
            Extensivity is the analogue for coherent categories of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+category"} exactness
            for regular categories. A coherent category which is both extensive and exact is called a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopos"} pretopos
          %h3#the_coherent_topology The coherent topology
          %p
            Any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+category"} coherent category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            admits a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcanonical+site"} subcanonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
            in which the covering families are generated by finite, jointly
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+epimorphism"} regular-epimorphic
            families: the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+coverage"} coherent coverage
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+epimorphisms"} regular epimorphisms
            and by finite unions of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensive+category"} extensive
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superextensive+site"} superextensive
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a pretopos, then its self-indexing is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            for its coherent topology. Exactness and extensivity are stronger than necessary, however; a pair of necessary and sufficient conditions for this to hold are that
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\;\rightrightarrows\; A
                is a kernel pair, then for any
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi B
                        %mo →
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon B\to A
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mi R
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*R \;\rightrightarrows\; B
                is also a kernel pair (this is equivalent to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain+fibration"} codomain fibration
                being a stack for the regular topology).
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo ↣
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,B \rightarrowtail C
                are a pair of subobjects, then for any
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X\to A
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\colon Y\to B
                and any isomorphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∩
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≅
                        %msup
                          %mi g
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∩
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*(A\cap B) \cong g^*(A\cap B)
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi f
                                %mo *
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi A
                              %mo ∩
                              %mi B
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Y
                            %mtd
                              %munder
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                            %mtd
                              %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{f^*(A\cap B) &amp; \overset{}{\to} &amp; X\\
                      \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow\\
                      Y&amp; \underset{}{\to} &amp; Z}
              %p exists and is also a pullback.
          %p
            Topoi of sheaves for coherent topologies on coherent categories are called
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+topos"} coherent topoi
          %h3#making_categories_coherent Making categories coherent
          %p
            Just like the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reg%2Flex+completion"} reg/lex completion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+complete+category"} finitely complete category
            into a coherent one in a universal way.
          %p
            Similarly, there are “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopos+completion"}> pretopos completion
            s” analogous to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ex%2Freg+completion"} ex/reg completion
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ex%2Flex+completion"} ex/lex completion
          %h3#SlicesAndInternalLogic Subobjects, slices and internal logic
          %p
            For any object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in a coherent category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset+of+subobjects"} poset of subobjects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sub
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub_{\mathcal{C}}(X)
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+lattice"} distributive lattice
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
            any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mi Sub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Sub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^* : Sub(Y) \to Sub(X)
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exists_f : Sub(X) \to Sub(Y)
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum"} dependent sum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/existential+quantifier"} existential quantifier
            along
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          %p
            The corresponding
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+category"} indexed category
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sub
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi DistLat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Sub : \mathcal{C}^{op} \to DistLat
          %p
            to the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+lattices"} distributive lattices
            is the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+hyperdoctrine"} coherent hyperdoctrine
            of the coherent category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          %h3#topos_of_types Topos of types
          %p
            See
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+of+types"} topos of types
